  partName: Spark Plug Cables
  description: The Spark Plug Cables are located at the top-center-center of the
    rocket engine and are made of a unique hair-like material, which provides electrical
    insulation and flexibility. They play a crucial role in igniting the fuel mixture,
    and their complex shape allows them to navigate through the engine's compact
    design. Interestingly, the spark plug cables are designed to withstand extremely
    high temperatures and pressures, making them a critical component of the engine's
    ignition system.
